DERIVED CODE
================================================================================

No third-party code has been incorporated into this project at this time.

When code is reused, it must be listed here AND carry a per-file header naming
the origin project, author, licence, commit hash and the nature of the
modification. Add the entry at the moment of copying.

Note on what changed with the move to GPL-3.0-or-later: GPL-3.0 projects are now
LICENCE-COMPATIBLE with this one, where under Apache-2.0 they were not. The
clean-room policy stands anyway, as a choice about where this project's code
comes from rather than a legal necessity. Anything incorporated in future must
still be recorded here, with its origin and licence, at the moment of copying.


================================================================================
INSPIRATION -- NO CODE REUSED
================================================================================

The projects below shaped this product's feature set. Their source has NOT been
read and NOT been reused; the designs here are clean-room, from feature lists,
documentation and forum threads.

Exi for SwiftKey -- Nordskog, GPL-3.0
  https://github.com/Nordskog/SwiftKeyExi
  Established the advanced keyboard-interaction feature set (cursor gestures,
  text selection, editor shortcuts, undo/redo). Lost Xposed's Text Engine is a
  clean-room design operating at the InputConnection layer rather than hooking
  a specific keyboard.

XPrivacy and XPrivacyLua -- Marcel Bokhorst (M66B), GPL-3.0
  https://github.com/M66B/XPrivacy
  https://github.com/M66B/XPrivacyLua
  Established the "return plausible fake data rather than deny" principle that
  informs Spoof Profiles.

AppOpsXposed -- jclehner, GPL-3.0
  https://github.com/jclehner/AppOpsXposed
  Established the case for surfacing Android's hidden AppOps to users.

GravityBox -- Peter Gregus (C3C076@xda), Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/GravityBox/GravityBox
  The grant is in that project's NOTICE file and in per-file headers, which is
  why GitHub's licence detector does not report it. Apache-2.0 makes it
  readable and reusable here; nothing has been taken from it so far.

Xposed Framework -- rovo89
  The original framework this ecosystem is built on.

LSPosed and Vector
  https://github.com/LSPosed/LSPosed
  https://github.com/JingMatrix/Vector
  GPL-3.0 runtime hosts. This module is loaded by them; it does not link their
  code and compiles only against the Apache-2.0 libxposed API.
